+# Gate E.1 — Identity, evidence and governance gaps
+
+2026-10-29. Findings below describe code behavior. They do not assert that a particular live lecturer, source claim or reviewer decision is wrong. R-01…R-18 classifications are in `REQUIREMENT_IMPLEMENTATION_MATRIX.csv`; all existing repository tests cited here are inspected / NOT_EXECUTED.
+
+## Essential invariants versus research vocabulary
+
+The application need not literally adopt T1–T6 as enum names or numeric weights. It must retain observations sufficient to distinguish target-slot publisher ORCID, registry DOI membership, Scopus-profile ORCID, raw source ORCID and aggregator entities; supporting and contrary signals must coexist. A registry not listing a DOI is incomplete evidence, not proof of a different person. A same-name coauthor can share a DOI; no tier should silently create an approved identity.
+
+The corrected tiers in `docs/qa/gate_d4/errata/EVIDENCE_ERRATA_D4_20261029.md` are: T1 target-slot publisher ORCID + registry DOI claim; T2 publisher ORCID without registry support or shifted position; T3 registry + full name; T4 registry + initials; T5 name + affiliation; T6 name. T1 verifies a research author-slot chain, not a human decision or all publications of an ID. COAUTHOR_CLAIM is not target identity support. The 13 cases with conflict indicators and the one CONFLICTING_EVIDENCE research classification are separate measures.
+
+Literal tiers, ranking thresholds, hard-versus-soft DOI conflict policy, publication exclusions and review permissions are owner design decisions. Lossless provenance, no arbitrary collision selection, no automatic acceptance and explicit evidence limitations are integrity requirements.
+
+## Confirmed unsafe code paths
+
+| ID / priority | Code evidence and trigger | Demonstrated behavior / business impact | Smallest safe remediation and test |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| G01 / P0 | `backend/app/services/lecturer_dataset/known_publication_ingestion.py:335-351`, `_build_lecturer_index()` uses `setdefault`; `383-415`, `490-497` never records URL ambiguity | Two canonical lecturers sharing a repository URL silently map to whichever row arrives first. No unique URL constraint in `backend/app/models/master_lecturer.py:82-115`. Exact-method synthetic probe reproduced first-row selection. Live collision presence NOT_VERIFIABLE. | URL→set mapping, explicit ambiguous error, wrapper refuses apply. Test TC-10; preserve both canonical people and all raw records. |
+| G02 / P0 | `backend/app/services/author_affiliation.py:194-218`, `parse_openalex_authorships()` prefers entity display_name and reads entity ORCID; `273-324`, `align_paper()` trusts ORCID→Scopus bridge without name/slot equality | Aggregator entity data can make an external authorship VERIFIED and carry its affiliations to a Scopus slot even when raw name disagrees. In-memory probe reproduced this. It does **not** create a LecturerScopusIdentity; impact is falsely trusted affiliation and downstream UI/coverage. | Keep raw_author_name separate; entity ORCID must not verify a slot. Restrict identifier proof by source type and retain conflicting observations. TC-03/04/15/19. Do not disable legitimate publisher identifier bridges merely to force same-name matching. |
+| G03 / P0 | `backend/app/services/normalization/scopus_author_normalizer.py:454-478`, `_ensure_publication_author_link()` returns for an existing pair before comparing order | EID/author replay at another position is counted as existing, with no position-drift error. Affiliation workflow later takes newest raw cells (`backend/app/services/affiliation_workflow.py:78-96`) while canonical order can remain older. Checks in affiliation importer may reject some drift, but canonical replay itself does not report it. | Compare existing order; keep canonical link, append structured conflict. TC-05/18. Existing `test_author_order_conflict_no_overwrite` covers a different author occupying a slot, not this branch. |
+| G04 / P0 | `backend/app/services/normalization/scopus_author_normalizer.py:398-414`, `445-452`, `497-510`; called in the batch loop `658-693` | IntegrityError recovery calls whole-session `rollback()` and resumes as existing/reused, without a savepoint or full batch restart. Earlier uncommitted successful writes in the batch can be rolled back while in-memory counters remain incremented. Other integrity failures can be swallowed by variant/link handlers. Conditional error-path defect; no concurrent DB reproduction was performed. | Follow publication normalizer's nested-savepoint pattern (`backend/app/services/normalization/scopus_normalizer.py:560-597`) and classify only expected uniqueness conflicts; otherwise fail/retry the batch with consistent counters. TC-18 plus fault injection and isolated-DB concurrency test. |
+
+P0 denotes code-level misattribution or data-loss exposure when its trigger occurs, not a declaration of exploited vulnerability or corrupt current data. G02/G03 map directly to research invariants; G01/G04 are import safety dependencies rather than invented R-19/R-20 requirements.
+
+## Missing or partial capabilities, not automatically bugs
+
+| ID | Classification / requirements | Verified boundary and gap |
+|---|---|---|
+| G05 | MISSING source-claim workflow; R-05/06/14/15/18 | Structured parser's allowlist is its current master-data contract. Craw raw capture is publication-linked only. Neither parses the 83/69 inventories or keeps source primary/count/disposition independently. `backend/app/services/lecturer_dataset/parser.py:338-375`; `backend/scripts/ingest_craw_known_publications.py:81-124`. |
+| G06 | PARTIAL frozen provenance; R-04/10/13 | EID/DOI, candidate author, source snapshot and known publication are preserved. Candidate snapshot retains external ID (`backend/app/services/matching/candidate_persistence.py:317-355`, `398-417`). `PublicationEvidence` omits author order and publication-author row ID (`backend/app/services/matching/candidate_types.py:67-87`). Affiliation resolutions **do** separately store external position and link to publication-author row (`backend/app/services/affiliation_import.py:76-93`, `258-291`); this does not repair candidate decision snapshots. |
+| G07 | PARTIAL conflicts; R-12/16 | Publication reconciliation emits DOI/title ambiguity/conflict records (`backend/app/services/matching/publication_evidence_enricher.py:91-193`), but generation returns only a count and persists candidates (`backend/app/services/matching/generation_workflow.py:131-149`). Promoted candidate evidence is always SUPPORTS (`backend/app/services/candidate_review_service.py:479-504`). Contrary evidence model capability exists, but no research-conflict producer/queue contract was found. |
+| G08 | PARTIAL absence semantics | No raw claim disappearance lifecycle. Candidate/current-observation queries retain prior pair observations even if absent from a later global generation (`backend/app/services/candidate_review_queries.py:22-83`). All historical known publications feed generation (`backend/app/services/matching/generation_workflow.py:87-101`). Preserve decisions; add explicit source-presence/staleness observations rather than auto-revoking. |
+| G09 | MISSING publication-specific review; R-01 | Approved Scopus ID implies all canonical publications of the ID in lecturer views and export links: `backend/app/services/lecturer_scopus_projection.py:305-329`, `backend/app/services/publication_queries.py:263-292`, `backend/app/services/publication_export.py:91-140`. No per-lecturer publication flag/exclusion is checked. A mixed-profile suspicion cannot be resolved at paper granularity. |
+| G10 | MISSING compensating identity review | `backend/app/schemas/review_api.py:11-25` / `backend/app/api/v1/endpoints/reviews.py:578-612` accept only ACCEPT/REJECT; `backend/app/services/review_service.py:6-17` is a stub. Schema REVOKED/REOPEN values and history filters are not operational transitions. Affiliation override revoke is unrelated. |
+| G11 | PARTIAL DOI/title policy; R-12 | `backend/app/services/matching/publication_evidence_enricher.py:125-193` allows title fallback when no DOI match exists, even if both source/canonical DOIs differ. `backend/tests/unit/test_publication_evidence_enricher.py:95-108` intentionally expects this. Record disagreement next to TITLE_EXACT; owner decides hard-block policy. Do not call an intentional tested fallback a confirmed bug without an agreed invariant. |
+| G12 | PARTIAL count semantics; R-09/11 | EID is globally unique and personal sets DISTINCT; global dashboard counts every local Publication (`backend/app/services/dashboard_queries.py:30-33`, `94-130`). This is deduplicated corpus count, not necessarily approved ICTU output. No source-claim count/time comparison exists. Preserve separate corpus, approved lecturer and institutional-affiliation scopes. |
+| G13 | PARTIAL name retrieval; R-07/17 | Canonical generator uses ordered exact/folded/comma/hyphen strings and leading title whitelist (`backend/app/services/matching/candidate_generator.py:28-90`, `114-149`, `207-253`). Craw adds anchored token correspondence (`backend/app/services/matching/craw_assisted_discovery.py:180-243`). Embedded “Master/Ts”, merged tokens and initials are not comprehensively normalized. Weak candidate recall needs tests before broader matching; absence of auto-accept is a protection. |
+| G14 | MISSING profile observations; R-08 | No Scopus Preview fetch-attempt/time-state ingestion found in active imports/matching. Does not infer MERGED from failures, but also cannot retain/retry the research observations in application state. |
+| G15 | PARTIAL audit atomicity | Craw success audit follows committed data (`backend/app/services/lecturer_dataset/craw_ingestion_workflow.py:133-176`), unlike atomic affiliation apply. Make success audit/data atomic if audit completeness is required; test audit-commit failure. Application append-only conventions are not a demonstrated deployed DB immutability barrier. |
+| G16 | PARTIAL rule provenance | Generator has seven name rules (`backend/app/services/matching/candidate_generator.py:39-47`), but source-state name rule list has four and version describes name/enrichment only (`backend/app/services/matching/candidate_persistence.py:42-59`, `178-190`). Craw-assisted discovery is not separately versioned in that list. Evidence stores each actual rule ID, limiting impact; align run metadata/version with actual executable retrieval for reproducible replays. |
+
+## Evidence channels that already work
+
+Affiliation alignment preserves full author arrays and multiple affiliation strings/organization entries (`backend/app/services/author_affiliation.py:194-239`, `273-344`), with reasons distinguishing no list, count/name mismatch and identifier conflict. Affiliation importer checks EID/Scopus ID/order/DOI against the canonical slot and withholds trusted links if another source reports ID_CONFLICT/ID_AMBIGUOUS (`backend/app/services/affiliation_import.py:150-178`, `248-319`). These protections should be reused, not described as entirely missing.
+
+ORCID bridge here reads registry **external identifiers**, not DOI works (`backend/app/services/affiliation_online_fetch.py:229-258`, `backend/app/services/affiliation_sources.py:223-228`, `303-319`). It is a different proof from T1. No active lecturer matcher consumes publisher email, ORCID works, profile affiliation, coauthor confirmation or literal evidence weights; `matching/rules/*` and scorer scaffolds are not counted as implementations. Email in the master importer only resolves lecturer records.
+
+## Frontend consequences
+
+| User concept | Existing representation | Gap |
+|---|---|---|
+| Source-listed claim | No typed source-claim API/UI | Missing IDs, especially zero-CSV/unowned IDs, cannot be reviewed as source claims |
+| Pending / approved | Queue status and approved identity cards distinguish them | Keep this boundary when claims are introduced |
+| Independent evidence | `frontend/src/pages/Publications/LinkEvidence.tsx:30-60` separates approval and evidence | `ORCID_EXACT` is too coarse for future source-tier proof; no active candidate ORCID producer currently promotes it |
+| Conflict / missing | Queue handles stale/ownership errors (`frontend/src/pages/ApprovalQueue/index.tsx:88-95`, `378-439`); affiliation UI shows detailed reasons (`frontend/src/pages/Publications/AuthorAffiliations.tsx:48-73`) | Research counter-evidence is not in candidate detail contract (`backend/app/schemas/review_api.py:93-121`) |
+| Affiliation verified | UI explains ORCID→Scopus bridge (`AuthorAffiliations.tsx:18-40`) | Label can overstate unsafe OpenAlex entity path; fix backend proof first, then scope label |
+| Multi-ID / counts | Approved identities and distinct personal publications exist | No source primary flag, profile-count snapshots or institutional eligibility filter |
+| REVOKE / REOPEN | History vocabulary includes REOPEN; affiliation override supports revoke | No canonical identity action in API or queue |
+
+## Areas requiring further verification
+
+Actual DB row counts, imported source coverage, deployed migrations/privileges, real URL collisions, race frequency, external-source quality, browser rendering and restore/backup behavior were not verified. No statement of “410 imported”, “152 available in application”, “all reviewer decisions protected by DB triggers” or “all publication counts are correct ICTU output” is supported by this audit alone. No real Scopus merge or identity decision occurred.
